  "text": "In July 2021, ten of us said \"green new deal,\" our most-repeated phrase, peaking on 2021-07-01. Six of us said \"green new deal mandates\" that same day. Six of us said \"the invest in america act.\" Six of us reached \"the hyde amendment\" on 2021-07-29, and six said \"of management and budget\" on 2021-07-14. Six of us said \"around the world\" on 2021-07-21. And six of us, in the same register, said \"look forward to working with\" and \"i'm proud to,\" each peaking on 2021-07-01.\n\nWe did not originate these lines. The record dates \"green new deal\" to 2019-01-03, \"the invest in america act\" to 2019-04-10, \"the hyde amendment\" to 2013-05-26. We repeated what was already in circulation. This is the shape of our month: a short list of phrases, six or ten of us at a time, converging on a single day.",
